import json,html
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(r'D:\Masters\signed_water_enhancement_20261023')
jobs=json.loads((ROOT/'jobs.json').read_text());checks=json.loads((ROOT/'project_checks.json').read_text());missing=json.loads((ROOT/'coverage_exclusions.json').read_text());rasters=json.loads((ROOT/'raster_manifest.json').read_text())
rows=[]
for c in checks:
 js=[j for j in jobs if j['project']==c['project'] and j['scene'] in c['scenes']]
 rows.append('<tr><td>'+html.escape(Path(c['project']).parent.name)+'</td><td>'+str(len(js))+'</td><td>'+', '.join(j['scene'] for j in js)+'</td><td>'+str(c['added_layers'])+'</td><td>'+str(len(c['preexisting_invalid_layers']))+'</td></tr>')
excluded=''.join('<tr><td>'+html.escape(Path(m['project']).parent.name)+'</td><td>'+m['scene']+'</td><td>'+html.escape(m['reason'])+'</td></tr>' for m in missing)
size=sum(Path(r['path']).stat().st_size for r in rasters)/1024**3
summary=dict(updated_projects=len(checks),enhanced_scene_entries=sum(len(c['scenes']) for c in checks),new_layers=sum(c['added_layers'] for c in checks),raster_patches=len(rasters),raster_size_gib=size,fully_excluded_batches=sorted({Path(m['project']).parent.name for m in missing}-{Path(c['project']).parent.name for c in checks}))
(ROOT/'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))
page='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Signed water-relative SAR enhancement</title><style>body{max-width:1150px;margin:40px auto;font:16px/1.6 system-ui;color:#182735;padding:20px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}td,th{padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd5dd;text-align:left}img{max-width:100%}.box{padding:20px;background:#edf4f8;border-radius:8px}h1{line-height:1.2}code{background:#eef1f5;padding:2px}</style><h1>Signed water-relative SAR enhancement</h1><p>Fixed v1 • native pixel grids • both dark and bright departures retained</p><div class="box"><b>Open your usual batch.qgz.</b> Expand <b>Signed water-relative SAR | fixed v1</b>, enable the group, choose an acquisition and display one enhancement at a time. Start with <b>VV 150 m: signed contrast (dB)</b>. Blue = darker than the surrounding mapped water; white = similar; red = brighter. The group starts off to preserve your current map. If a project was already open, preserve pending edits and reload it from disk to see the new layers.</div>'''
page+=f'<p>Updated {summary["updated_projects"]} batch projects with {summary["enhanced_scene_entries"]} scene entries and {summary["new_layers"]} validated new layers. Raster output: {size:.2f} GiB. Every changed project has a timestamped backup. Original layer references and checked states were preserved; vector outlines are ordered above the new rasters.</p>'
page+='''<h2>Interpretation</h2><p><code>signed contrast = pixel dB − surrounding-water mean dB</code><br><code>standardized contrast = signed contrast / max(water SD, 1 dB)</code></p><p>Fixed square-annulus half-widths: 150 m outside / 50 m guard, and 500 m outside / 150 m guard. Display limits stay at ±6 dB or ±3 standardized units. Numeric raster values are not clipped. Background mean, spread, support fraction and original unsmoothed dB are provided under diagnostics.</p><p>ESA WorldCover 2021 v200 class 80 defines mapped water, with a 30 m exclusion next to nonwater or unknown cells. At least 70% annulus support and 30 valid water pixels are required. Unsupported contrast is NoData. This annual land-cover map is a water proxy; nearshore inaccuracies, ships, wakes and fronts can affect the estimate. These layers are descriptive aids, not plastic probabilities or proof of improved annotation. No plastic labels, CMEMS values or fitted classifier determine their values. Instrument noise correction remains separate.</p><p>Coverage is the observation/search and annotation work areas plus 1 km context, with one context-only batch using its wider AOI. Full Sentinel-1 swaths have not been processed. Manila uses recovered local calibrated VV/VH. Original inputs and annotation datasets were not edited.</p><p><a href="README.md">Full method and usage notes</a> · <a href="method.json">Frozen settings</a> · <a href="algorithm_checks.json">Algorithm checks</a> · <a href="raster_checks.json">Raster checks</a> · <a href="project_checks.json">Project checks and backups</a></p><h2>Visual check</h2><p>At the fixed Greece deployment footprints, 55 of 60 pixel centres have support in the 150 m view. None has sufficient support in the 500 m view because of nearby land. This is an eligibility check, not target detection. Missing values remain blank. <a href="deployment_support_check.json">Support counts by acquisition</a>.</p><img src="signed_enhancement_preview.png"><h2>Updated batches</h2><table><tr><th>Batch</th><th>Scenes</th><th>Acquisitions</th><th>Added layers</th><th>Already broken layers</th></tr>'''
page+=''.join(rows)+'</table><h2>Coverage exclusions</h2><p>Pre-existing missing data is recorded rather than fabricated. Other local texture/decomposition bands cannot replace calibrated VV/VH for this calculation.</p><table><tr><th>Batch</th><th>Scene</th><th>Reason</th></tr>'+excluded+'</table><p>Water-mask provenance: <a href="https://esa-worldcover.org/en/data-access">ESA WorldCover 10 m 2021 v200</a>, CC BY 4.0. Cached class and eligibility masks retain source URLs. The earlier historical coastline mask was rejected during visual QA and is not used in these layers.</p>'
(ROOT/'REPORT.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8');print(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))
